there's a good reason why the new Mad  Max game occasionally resembles this  year's Mad Max fury road  it's a canonical prequel that pits you  against scabrous scrotus son of the  film's sinister immortan joe driving is  central to life in the wasteland and is  the basis for the game's best moments -  the combination of an intriguing world  and great car combat makes playing Mad  Max an occasional joy but shallow ground  combat and a handful of other missteps  ultimately lead to disappointment at the  start of the game scrotus and a pack of  his gangly war boys steal your beloved  car the Interceptor leaving you  empty-handed  however fortune smiles upon you in a  golem like mechanic by the name of Chum  Bucket crosses your path and joins your  fight he's a whiz with both a wrench and  a harpoon making him the perfect  companion in the hard driving and  violent wasteland while you're on the  road it's normal to be confronted by  three or four enemy cars at once and  there's some carry enemies that will try  to hop onto your car you can resort to  your trusty shotgun or pull over and  fight it out with your fists watching  max manhandle thugs can be entertaining  but the combat controls are rudimentary  at best we're mashing 1 button dishes  out contextual attacks and another  parries attacks when an enemy has an  icon flashing over their head the combat  system is so simple at its core that  nearly every fight can be won by  alternatively tapping attack and parry  save for a few boss fights when you have  to roll out of harm's way  it's a none rewarding experience overall  that's far too easy to exploit  oh wait James don't get too excited we  need to get the hell out of here oh the  story progresses as max upgrades his car  with new parts either by completing  fetch quests or dismantling enemy  outposts on foot after a new part is  unlocked you purchase it using scrap  metal that you collect around the world  which you primarily acquire from glowing  piles that are sparingly strewn about  the wasteland these piles include  massive car parts which you can  conveniently stick in your pocket it's  helpful that you can carry multiple cars  worth of metal on your person but it  doesn't make much sense  max can increase his efficiency as a  scavenger by trading in coins to a  mystic that resides on top of certain  cliffs he's an odd duck  but like Chum his peculiarities add to  the world's mythology in a great way  though some of his gifts diminish the  threat of the wasteland by artificially  boosting your gathering abilities Mad  Max is rife with logical inconsistencies  that pull you out of the world and  negate your supposed struggle to survive  being run over by a car should  theoretically kill you outright but  you're damaged more by the punch of a  withered nomad than by the mass of a  three-ton war machine if you're a sloppy  fighter a few punches is all it takes to  bite the dust but you can somehow enjoy  getting run over by a car five or six  times before you have to worry about  your health in fact you get so good at  being struck by cars that you eventually  learn unofficially how to jump onto the  windshield of an oncoming vehicle to  perform a triple misty flip and land  gracefully on your feet you can also  apparently stand in fire without getting  hurt but only sometimes experience has  taught me that a burning car isn't as  hot as a flamethrower though you're told  that you need to collect vital resources  such as water and food I never noticed  any gradual deleterious impacts to my  health for me exposed to the wasteland  if anything these resources were used  for recovering health after a  particularly challenging vehicle battle  bad max where it's then sooner rather  than later as quests become more  repetitive in the wasteland more  unbelievable thankfully the final battle  forces you to chase down a convoy and  dismantle scrotus his massive war rig  regular car combat is fun but the scale  of the war rig and the relentless nature  of scrotus is horde make this battle  truly memorable the promise of a Mad Max  game is participating in its harsh  reality this Mad Max with over game  design flaws and a lack of consistency  fails to properly capture the true  spirit of the wasteland or Max's  character it's a shame because the world  is beautiful grim and fascinating some  interesting characters impressive  environments and great car combat draw  you in and incentivize you to keep going  but it's when you get out of the car  that things begin to fall apart combat  system is too dumbed down to enjoy and  repetitive activities get old very fast  Mad Max is too focused on providing you  with an open world that's filled with  missions and not focused enough on  making those missions worth playing  gonna hurry up
 

